---
// Diagnostic page — a place to SEE the Instagram embed behaviour first-hand.
// DJ asked for a page where a working IG embed lives so he can see exactly what
// the "black bars" issue is. This renders the OFFICIAL Instagram embed (blockquote
// + embed.js) untouched — the same markup Meta hands you — next to notes on what is
// and isn't fixable, and a side-by-side of the self-hosted alternative.
// Not linked in the nav; reach it at /lab/ig-embed.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<title>IG embed check · Monuments</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wdth,wght@12..96,75..100,300..800&family=Fragment+Mono:ital@0;1&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style is:global>
:root{
  --ink:#161514; --paper:#F5F3EF; --rose:#EFA1AD; --cobalt:#2438E8; --red:#E0311A;
  --dim:#8f8d88; --line:#dcd9d2; --lined:#2c2b29;
  --wrap:1380px; --pad:clamp(22px,4.6vw,44px);
  --disp:'Bricolage Grotesque',sans-serif; --dispw:800;
  --mono:'Fragment Mono',monospace;
  --spark:var(--rose); --struct:var(--cobalt);
}
*{margin:0;box-sizing:border-box}
body{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);font-family:var(--disp);font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;overflow-x:hidden}
.mono{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:400}
.wrap{max-width:var(--wrap);margin:0 auto;padding-left:var(--pad);padding-right:var(--pad)}
a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}

.corners{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:60;pointer-events:none;mix-blend-mode:difference}
.corners span{position:absolute;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff}
.corners .c1{top:20px;left:38px;pointer-events:auto}
.corners .c1 b{font-family:var(--disp);font-weight:var(--dispw);font-size:34px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.corners .c1 i{font-style:normal;color:#fff;display:inline-block;animation:spin 7s linear infinite}
.corners .c2{top:26px;right:22px;pointer-events:auto}
.corners .c2 a{font-size:15px;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-left:22px;position:relative;padding-bottom:3px}
.corners .c2 a::after{content:'';position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:1.5px;background:currentColor;transform:scaleX(0);transform-origin:right;transition:transform .42s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)}
.corners .c2 a:hover::after{transform:scaleX(1);transform-origin:left}
.corners .c3{bottom:20px;left:22px}
.corners .c4{bottom:20px;right:22px}
@keyframes spin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}}

/* page */
.head{padding:clamp(120px,20vh,200px) 0 clamp(40px,7vh,70px)}
.head .kick{color:var(--spark);margin-bottom:22px}
.head h1{font-weight:var(--dispw);font-size:clamp(40px,7vw,92px);line-height:.92;letter-spacing:-.035em}
.head h1 .serif{font-family:'Instrument Serif',serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.head p{max-width:60ch;margin-top:24px;color:#cbc8c2;font-size:clamp(16px,1.5vw,19px)}
.head p b{color:var(--paper);font-weight:600}

.legend{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:18px;margin:44px 0 10px}
.legend .box{border:1px solid var(--lined);padding:20px 20px 22px;background:#1c1b1a}
.legend .box .t{color:var(--spark);margin-bottom:10px}
.legend .box.bad .t{color:var(--red)}
.legend .box.ok .t{color:#7ec98f}
.legend .box p{font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#cbc8c2}

.demos{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:clamp(24px,3.4vw,48px);padding:36px 0 20px;align-items:start}
.demo{border:1px solid var(--lined);background:#1a1918;padding:16px 16px 22px}
.demo .cap{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px;color:var(--dim)}
.demo .cap b{color:var(--paper);font-weight:400}
.demo .cap .tag{color:var(--red)}
.demo .cap .tag.ok{color:#7ec98f}
/* frame the embed so the letterboxing IG adds is obvious against a bright edge */
.demo .stage{background:#000;position:relative;border:1px dashed rgba(224,49,26,.5)}
.demo .stage .note{position:absolute;left:8px;top:8px;z-index:5;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);background:rgba(22,21,20,.72);padding:3px 6px;pointer-events:none}
.instagram-media{margin:0 auto!important}

.note-self{margin:30px 0 clamp(80px,14vh,140px);border-left:2px solid var(--spark);padding:6px 0 6px 22px;max-width:74ch}
.note-self .mono{color:var(--spark);margin-bottom:10px}
.note-self p{color:#cbc8c2;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7}
.note-self p+p{margin-top:12px}

footer{border-top:1px solid var(--lined);padding:34px 0 18px}
footer .row{display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:baseline;gap:8px 22px;flex-wrap:wrap}
footer .blk{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--dim)}

@media (max-width:640px){.corners .c2{display:none}}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="corners">
  <span class="c1"><a href="/"><b>M<i>✳</i>NUMENTS</b></a></span>
  <span class="c2"><a href="/work">Work</a><a href="/about">About</a></span>
  <span class="c3">INTERNAL · IG-EMBED CHECK</span>
  <span class="c4" id="clock">LA --:--</span>
</div>

<div class="wrap head">
  <div class="kick mono">Internal · not linked in nav</div>
  <h1>The Instagram <span class="serif">embed</span>, unfiltered.</h1>
  <p>These are <b>real, live Instagram embeds</b> — the exact blockquote + <span class="mono" style="font-size:13px">embed.js</span> markup Meta hands you, untouched by any of our CSS. This is so you can see the thing I keep flagging with your own eyes. Look at the <b>black bars</b> above and below the video, and the Instagram header/footer chrome. That framing is rendered <b>inside Instagram's own iframe</b>, on their servers. We can't reach into it to crop or recolor it — it's cross-origin, so any CSS we write stops at the iframe's edge.</p>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="legend">
    <div class="box bad">
      <div class="t mono">The black bars</div>
      <p>IGTV / vertical posts get letterboxed to fit IG's fixed player box. Those bars live inside their iframe — no CSS of ours can remove them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="box bad">
      <div class="t mono">The chrome</div>
      <p>The profile header, caption, like/comment row and "view on Instagram" footer are Meta's. They come with the embed and can't be stripped.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="box ok">
      <div class="t mono">What we control</div>
      <p>Only the box <em>around</em> the embed — width, centering, background, spacing. Everything you see rendered by Instagram itself is off-limits.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="demos">
    <div class="demo">
      <div class="cap mono"><b>IGTV · 16:9 in a vertical box</b> <span class="tag">letterboxed</span></div>
      <div class="stage">
        <span class="note">← black bars are IG's</span>
        <blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/tv/CHx63BgpiYr/?utm_source=ig_embed" data-instgrm-version="14" style="background:#FFF;border:0;border-radius:3px;box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.15);margin:0 auto;max-width:540px;min-width:280px;padding:0;width:100%"></blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="demo">
      <div class="cap mono"><b>Reel · vertical native</b> <span class="tag ok">fits better</span></div>
      <div class="stage">
        <span class="note" style="color:#7ec98f">vertical sits cleaner</span>
        <blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/reel/Cl9hIJ-vS-b/?utm_source=ig_embed" data-instgrm-version="14" style="background:#FFF;border:0;border-radius:3px;box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.15);margin:0 auto;max-width:540px;min-width:280px;padding:0;width:100%"></blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="demo">
      <div class="cap mono"><b>IGTV · second reference</b> <span class="tag">letterboxed</span></div>
      <div class="stage">
        <span class="note">← same story here</span>
        <blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/tv/CIJ-YPVJVAq/?utm_source=ig_embed" data-instgrm-version="14" style="background:#FFF;border:0;border-radius:3px;box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.15);margin:0 auto;max-width:540px;min-width:280px;padding:0;width:100%"></blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note-self">
    <div class="mono">The alternative — and its trade-off</div>
    <p>The only way to kill the bars and the Instagram chrome is to <b>not use their embed at all</b>: pull the raw video, host it ourselves, and play it in our own clean frame (that's what the case-study grids and the reel snippets already do — no bars, no chrome, silent autoplay, full styling control).</p>
    <p>The catch: that path needs the source file, and Instagram blocks downloads unless you're logged in. I won't touch your account or cookies to do it. So for anything IG-only, you'd either send me the original export, or we accept Meta's framing and just present it as cleanly as we can around the edges — which is what this page is doing.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--spark)">Your call on which posts matter enough to dig up the source video for. Send me the raw files and I'll self-host them so they match everything else.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<footer>
  <div class="wrap row">
    <span class="blk">Monuments © MMXXVI · ELMT.NO.004259</span>
    <span class="blk">internal diagnostic</span>
  </div>
</footer>

<script is:inline async src="https://www.instagram.com/embed.js"></script>
<script is:inline>
(function(){
  var el=document.getElementById('clock');
  function t(){try{var s=new Date().toLocaleTimeString('en-US',{timeZone:'America/Los_Angeles',hour:'2-digit',minute:'2-digit',hour12:false});el.textContent='LA '+s;}catch(e){}}
  t();setInterval(t,20000);
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
